{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And Joshua weakened.</b> The word ויחלש testifies that the Holy One, blessed be He, does not destroy and annul the order of the stars entirely, nor does He coerce nature so that it cannot pursue its course and custom, except for a great need and a necessary matter — for the order and the workings of nature are His actions, and how could one come against His own action to uproot and destroy it? Rather, He, blessed be He, outwits the order to save whomever He wishes to save, adding and diminishing according to His will, in accordance with reward and punishment, without destroying the order. And this is the sense of ויחלש, for it did not say 'and he killed'; and the Holy One, blessed be He, saved Israel from the hand of Amalek, while the order was not destroyed. And thus we find that they expounded: 'Depart from your astrology — Abram does not beget, but Abraham begets.' And why would He not have made it so that Abram begets? Rather, in order that the order not be destroyed." "<b>And it is possible</b> to say further regarding ויחלש: that He weakened the strength of above, and it did not say 'Amalek' but 'et Amalek' — to include the prince of Amalek, whom Joshua weakened through his prayer, or through the lifting of Moses' hands, until the prince himself was helping Israel and came against Amalek."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:00:30.059022362Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}